          "aiContent": "Async chain mapping and error/timing analysis:\n\n- Async functions are used extensively for workflow steps, CLI commands, and file operations (e.g., workflow, step1_parallel, runCommand, executeStep17).\n- Error handling uses try/catch in CLI commands and step handlers, but some catch blocks lack explicit retry/fallback logic; network errors (including timeouts) are parsed and retried in ai_helpers.js, with exponential backoff for timeouts.\n- Timeout handling is robust: step execution uses Promise.race with setTimeout, timeouts are configurable per step, and execution timestamps are tracked with Date.now(); parallel operations use Promise.all and sequential awaits, minimizing race conditions. CORS/network errors are referenced in AI persona prompts but not directly handled in source code.",
          "report": "# Step 18: Debugging Analysis — Async Flow Debugger\n\n## Files Analyzed\n- eslint.config.js\n- jest.config.js\n- src/index.ts\n- src/utils/errors.ts\n- src/core/executor.ts\n- src/core/system.ts\n\n## AI Analysis\n\nAsync chain mapping and error/timing analysis:\n\n- Async functions are used extensively for workflow steps, CLI commands, and file operations (e.g., workflow, step1_parallel, runCommand, executeStep17).\n- Error handling uses try/catch in CLI commands and step handlers, but some catch blocks lack explicit retry/fallback logic; network errors (including timeouts) are parsed and retried in ai_helpers.js, with exponential backoff for timeouts.\n- Timeout handling is robust: step execution uses Promise.race with setTimeout, timeouts are configurable per step, and execution timestamps are tracked with Date.now(); parallel operations use Promise.all and sequential awaits, minimizing race conditions. CORS/network errors are referenced in AI persona prompts but not directly handled in source code.\n"
